-- title:
--   Minimal primes of the full-level moduli ring as relabelling translates
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero carrying a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ with level group the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\ell$, $M'$ units in $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the coefficientwise pushforward of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function. Assume the two equivariance hypotheses: level-$\ell$ data (two affine points with the $\ell$-division polynomial vanishing at their $x$-coordinates and both independence elements units) and $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-type kernel polynomials (degree and leading-coefficient normalisation, divisibility of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and the divisibility conditions on the `smulNumerator`s; the two-torsion case separately) transform correctly under Weierstrass variable changes. Assume further a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity, a level-$q$ transport $\mathcal{T}$ of raw Drinfeld pairs which is a section transport, and the existence of graded comparison homomorphisms of projective-model rings realising variable changes and coefficient changes (`hVC`, `hCO`). Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the rigidified moduli datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q …`, i.e. a finite-type $A$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point such that every point of the problem over an $A$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal point under a unique $A$-algebra map $B_0\to T$, the level data being the product of $\Gamma_0$-type kernel polynomials at the prime powers dividing $M'$, level-$\ell$ structures, and Drinfeld level-$q$ bases. Let $x$ be a point of the problem over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`, the $q$-expansion of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$; assume the $A$-subalgebra of $B_0$ generated by `P₀.j₀` is a domain, and that the classifying map $\iota_x=$ `P₀.classify x` $: B_0\to K$ is dense in the sense that every $k\in K$ is a ratio $\iota_x(a)/\iota_x(b)$ with $\iota_x(b)\neq 0$. Then for every minimal prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of the zero ideal of $B_0$ there is an $A$-algebra automorphism $e$ of $B_0$ fixing the $j$-invariant of the universal point such that $\mathfrak{p}$ is the preimage under $e$ of $\ker\iota_x$.
--
--   This is the transitivity statement for the geometric components of the full-level fine moduli ring: every irreducible component of $\operatorname{Spec} B_0$ is carried to the component cut out by the Tate-type point $x$ by one of the relabelling automorphisms of the moduli problem, which fix the $j$-invariant of the universal object. It feeds the combined statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.ker_classify_mem_minimalPrimes_and_forall_exists_algEquiv_comap_eq_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.ker_classify_mem_minimalPrimes_and_forall_exists_algEquiv_comap_eq_gamma0Pow), from which the identification of the components of the full-level modular curve with the q-expansion field is obtained.
